# Copy to .env.local for local work. On Vercel, set these under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Only THREE variables belong in this repository. Everything else — the
# database, the encryption keys, the Cloudinary secret, the Resend key — is
# backend-only and lives in Railway. Nothing here may hold a value that would
# be damaging to read, because anything in a Next.js app can end up in a
# server log or, if misprefixed, in the browser bundle.

# Canonical origin — drives metadataBase, canonical tags, sitemap.xml and
# robots.txt. No trailing slash. Leave unset to use the production domain
# baked into src/lib/site.ts.
# PUBLIC by design: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.bhargavihealthworld.com

# 🔴 REQUIRED FOR ANY BUILD SINCE D-042. The backend's origin.
#
# Read by the /api/contact proxy at request time, by the content generator at
# build time, and — since D-042 tranche 1 — by every public page, which now
# fetches its content from the backend through Next's tagged Data Cache instead
# of importing a committed snapshot.
#
#   Local:      http://localhost:3001   (run the backend: cd ../backend && npm run dev)
#   Production: the Railway URL, or the API subdomain once DNS is set
#
# ⚠ `npm run build` FAILS without it, and that is deliberate. Under D-016 a
# missing value meant "use the committed files and exit 0", which is how a
# production deploy could publish content weeks out of date with a green build.
# There is intentionally NO silent fallback. If you only need to typecheck or
# lint, those do not need the backend — only `build` and `start` do.
#
# ⚠ The nine migrated collections (services, testimonials, videos, gallery,
# faqs, jobs, statistics, content-lists, posts) come from here at runtime.
# Page copy, per-page SEO and site settings are still build-time generated
# (D-042b tranches 2 and 3), so they continue to need the generator.
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Shared with the backend. Exempts this trusted server-side caller and the
# build from the public rate limit.
# 🔴 SERVER-ONLY. Never rename this to NEXT_PUBLIC_* — that would publish it to
# every visitor. It is read only inside a route handler and the build script,
# neither of which ships to the browser.
# BACKEND_API_KEY=

# 🔴 THE PUBLISH CAPABILITY (D-042 / D-043). Authenticates POST /api/revalidate,
# which the backend calls after a content mutation to invalidate the affected
# cache tags. Must be the SAME value set on the Railway backend.
#
# Unset ⇒ /api/revalidate answers 503 and REFUSES every request. It never falls
# open: an unset secret must not mean "no authentication required".
#
# 🔴 SERVER-ONLY, and it is a capability — anyone holding it can force the live
# site to re-render. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never logged, scoped per environment
# so a staging backend cannot invalidate production.
# REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# --- Deliberately absent ----------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY      → backend only. The frontend never sends mail; it posts to
#                       /api/contact, and the backend notifies the clinic.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL    → 🔴 FORBIDDEN (decision D-034). Notification addresses are
#                       DATABASE ROWS (branches.notify_email, falling back to
#                       site_settings.default_notify_email) so the clinic can
#                       change them without a deploy. The backend's boot gate
#                       REFUSES TO START if this variable is set at all.
